    <node id="INFECTIONS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Infections are illnesses caused by pathogens, and they are commonly included in family history questions as part of medical assessments. In the context of cancer treatment, infections are also a frequent side effect of targeted therapy, and the body becomes particularly vulnerable to infections during high-dose chemotherapy. Thus, infections represent both a general category of disease and a specific clinical concern for patients undergoing certain cancer treatments.
Relationships:
  - Source: TARGETED THERAPY
    Target: INFECTIONS
    Description: Infections are a common side effect of targeted therapy
  - Source: HIGH-DOSE CHEMOTHERAPY
    Target: INFECTIONS
    Description: The body is very vulnerable to infections during high-dose chemotherapy
  - Source: INFECTIONS
    Target: FAMILY HISTORY
    Description: Family history questions include illnesses, infections, and injuries.</data>
