  Description: A biopsy is a diagnostic procedure that plays a central role in determining a patient’s diagnosis. It is specifically used to establish whether a tumor or lesion is benign or malignant, thereby helping to determine tumor status. By collecting and examining tissue samples, a biopsy provides critical information that supports and confirms a diagnosis, particularly in cases of suspected cancer. The results obtained from a biopsy are directly used in the diagnostic process, enabling clinicians to make informed decisions about the nature of the disease and subsequent treatment. In summary, biopsy is an essential diagnostic tool, and its findings are integral to the overall diagnosis, especially for confirming cancer and assessing tumor status. 
