    Description: NCCN Cancer Centers and the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) are both recognized resources for locating clinical trials. NCCN Cancer Centers are specifically listed as a resource for finding clinical trials within the United States, while the NLM provides the worldwide clinicaltrials.gov database. Together, these two entities offer complementary access to clinical trial information: NCCN Cancer Centers focus on U.S.-based cancer centers, and the NLM supplies a comprehensive, global database of clinical trials.</data>
