    <node id="HEALTH CARE PROVIDER (ENTITY ID: 35)">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">HEALTH CARE PROVIDER is a medical professional who delivers comprehensive patient care. This clinician, which includes doctors and other medical professionals, performs thorough physical examinations and checks vital signs, body systems, and lymph nodes. The health care provider also assesses height, weight, lungs, heart, eyes, ears, nose, throat, organs, and skin. In addition to conducting exams, the provider gives patients important information about next steps and treatment options. The health care provider (HCP) receives imaging reports from the radiologist and discusses the results with the patient, ensuring clear communication and follow-up care.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: A physician is a type of health care provider
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: The care team is a collaborative group that includes health care providers as integral members. Health care providers are part of the care team, serving as members who contribute to the team's overall function. In essence, the health care provider is a constituent of the care team, with both descriptions emphasizing that providers belong to and participate within the care team structure.
  - Source: PATIENT
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: The patient should discuss imaging test results with the health care provider
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Description: A health care provider is responsible for performing the physical exam, during which vital signs are also checked. The physical exam is carried out by the health care provider as part of the assessment process.
  - Source: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: A health care provider may perform a physical exam
  - Source: TREATMENT
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: A health care provider gives information about next steps and treatment.
  - Source: DOCTOR
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: A doctor is a type of health care provider
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN
  - Description: A primary care physician is a type of health care provider
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: NURSE
  - Description: A nurse is a type of health care provider
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: COMPLETE SKIN EXAM
  - Description: The health care provider conducts a complete skin exam during the physical exam
  - Source: RADIOLOGIST
  - Target: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Description: The radiologist writes an imaging report following an examination and sends it to the patient's health care provider. This report is a formal documentation of the radiologist's findings and interpretations. The health care provider receives this imaging report to inform patient care decisions. Thus, the radiologist and the health care provider are connected through the delivery of the written imaging report, ensuring that diagnostic information reaches the provider responsible for the patient's treatment.</data>
