    <node id="HOSPITAL (ENTITY ID: 478)">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A hospital is a medical institution that provides diagnostic, treatment, and specialized care services. It may offer specialized expertise in particular conditions, such as a patient’s subtype of acute myeloid leukemia (AML), tailoring its services to that specific diagnosis. Hospitals are equipped to perform surgical and diagnostic procedures, including excision biopsies, which involve the surgical removal of tissue for examination. As a setting for biopsy procedures, a hospital may or may not have a neuropathologist on staff; in cases where neuropathology expertise is unavailable or additional analysis is needed, tissue or biopsy samples can be sent to an external laboratory for comprehensive analysis. Thus, the hospital serves as a versatile medical facility capable of both direct patient care and coordination with specialized diagnostic laboratories.
Relationships: None present in the provided relationship table.</data>
