      <data key="d1">Heart tests, also known as cardiac tests, are medical evaluations used to assess how well the heart works, measure heart function before or during treatment, and monitor potential side effects of treatments. These tests include electrocardiogram (ECG) and echocardiogram, among others. They serve to evaluate the heart's overall condition and function.
