    <node id="PLASTIC SURGEON (ID: 834)">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Plastic surgeons are doctors who can remove cancer as well as reconstruct, restore, and repair body parts. They may work with a pathologist during surgery and are trained to close wounds after surgery, especially when deeper tissue is involved.

Relationships:
  - Source: PLASTIC SURGEON
  - Target: SURGERY
  - Description: Plastic surgeons perform surgery to remove cancer and to reconstruct, restore, and repair body parts (Relationship id: 2020)

  - Source: PLASTIC SURGEON
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The care team may include plastic surgeons (Relationship id: 2019)

  - Source: PATHOLOGIST
  - Target: PLASTIC SURGEON
  - Description: Plastic surgeons may work with a pathologist during surgery for more immediate results (Relationship id: 2018)

  - Source: PLASTIC SURGEON
  - Target: RECONSTRUCTIVE SURGERY
  - Description: Plastic surgeons are trained to reconstruct and restore the appearance of the affected area after cancer surgery (Relationship id: 2021)

