    <node id="ANAL DYSPLASIA">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Anal dysplasia is a precancerous condition characterized by the presence of abnormal, fast-growing cells in the anal canal or in the tissue near the anus. These lesions are considered precancerous, meaning that if left untreated, they have the potential to progress to anal cancer. Identifying and treating anal dysplasia is important because early intervention may help prevent the development of invasive anal cancer. The condition can be detected through specialized examination, particularly using high-resolution anoscopy, which allows for detailed visualization of the abnormal cellular changes. Overall, anal dysplasia represents a critical stage for medical monitoring and preventive treatment. 
Relationships:
  - Source: ANAL CANCER
  - Target: ANAL DYSPLASIA
  - Description: Anal dysplasia is a precancerous condition that may develop into anal cancer</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
