    <node id="PRIMARY LIVER CANCER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary liver cancer is cancer that originates in the liver. The most common type is hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). In adults, other types of primary liver cancer include intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma, sarcomas, and mixed-type tumors. 
Relationships (to HCC):
