    Description: Biopsy results and biopsy findings play a central role in guiding cancer treatment decisions. After a cancer diagnosis, these results are used to help plan the appropriate treatment approach. Additionally, biopsy findings provide specific information about which treatments the cancer may respond to, enabling more targeted and effective therapy. Together, biopsy and treatment are directly connected: the biopsy supplies essential diagnostic and predictive data, while treatment planning relies on that data to determine the best course of action for each patient. (Relationship 1910)
  - Source: TREATMENT
    Target: SURGERY
    Description: Surgery is a type of cancer treatment. (Relationship 88)
  - Source: SURGERY
    Target: TREATMENT
    Description: Surgery is a type of treatment, specifically a form of cancer treatment. It is one of the main treatment options available for cancer, including cervical cancer, where it is recognized as a primary treatment approach. Surgery can also be combined with other therapies; when drug therapy is administered before surgery, the pathologic stage of the disease may include a "y" prefix to indicate this sequence. As a treatment modality, surgery plays a key role in the management of cancer and is included among the main types of treatment for cervical cancer. (Relationship 1142)
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
    Target: TREATMENT
    Description: Treatment is given for cervical cancer, and options depend on the extent of the cancer and other factors. (Relationship 2351)
  - Source: TREATMENT
    Target: CHEMOTHERAPY
    Description: Chemotherapy is a form of medical treatment used primarily in oncology. As a cancer treatment, chemotherapy involves the use of cytotoxic drugs to destroy or inhibit the growth of cancer cells. It is applicable across multiple cancer types and is often integrated into broader therapeutic protocols. Specifically, chemotherapy is a recognized type of treatment for acute myeloid leukemia (AML), where it serves as the standard-of-care approach for managing this blood cancer. In addition to its role in AML, chemotherapy is also a component of cervical cancer treatment, frequently administered as part of chemoradiation—a combination of chemotherapy and radiation therapy that enhances the effectiveness of treatment. As such, chemotherapy occupies a central position within the overall category of cancer treatment, functioning both as a standalone modality and as an adjunct to other therapies. The entity TREATMENT encompasses a wide range of medical interventions, and chemotherapy is one of its key subtypes, distinguished by its mechanism of action and its established role in hematologic and solid tumor malignancies. Overall, chemotherapy exemplifies a targeted and evidence-based treatment option, with particular significance in AML, where it is the established standard of care, and in cervical cancer, where it is integrated into combined-modality regimens. (Relationship 86)
  - Source: TREATMENT
    Target: RADIATION THERAPY
    Description: Radiation therapy is a type of treatment that falls under the broader category of medical treatments. Specifically, it is a type of cancer treatment, used to address malignant diseases. Additionally, radiation therapy is a type of treatment for cervical cancer, indicating its application in managing that particular form of cancer. (Relationship 87)
