      <data key="d4">
**No relationships in the provided data connect DIAGNOSIS to specific symptoms or signs.** The data contain no symptom/sign entities linked to DIAGNOSIS, so this category is empty. (Symptoms are alluded to only indirectly in source text, e.g., asking patients about symptoms affecting quality of life during prostate cancer testing, but no symptom-to-diagnosis relationship records were provided [Data: Sources (210, 211)].)
</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LABORATORY TESTS AND PROCEDURES THAT CONFIRM OR EXCLUDE A DIAGNOSIS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">
The following tests and procedures have explicit relationships with DIAGNOSIS:

- **Biopsy** — key to confirming the diagnosis; a central diagnostic procedure for determining whether a lesion is benign or malignant [Data: Relationships (2708, 1762)].
- **Bone marrow biopsy** — used to confirm a diagnosis of AML [Data: Relationships (941)].
- **Bone marrow aspirate** — used to confirm a diagnosis of AML [Data: Relationships (938)].
- **CT scan** — helps confirm the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma; produces images used in cancer diagnostic testing [Data: Relationships (2712, 3014)].
- **MRI** — helps confirm the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma [Data: Relationships (2711)].
- **Imaging** — used in diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma; closely linked to diagnosis across cancer types, e.g., basal cell skin cancer [Data: Relationships (2710, 1867)].
- **Blood tests** — part of the diagnostic workup [Data: Relationships (2713)].
- **Neurological exam** — used in the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma [Data: Relationships (2709)].
- **Eye exam** — helps diagnose primary CNS lymphoma if the eyes are involved [Data: Relationships (2714)].
- **Skin exam** — part of the diagnosis process [Data: Relationships (2669)].
- **ctDNA testing** — considered after colon cancer diagnosis to predict recurrence risk [Data: Relationships (602)].
- **Cystoscopy and imaging** — diagnostic tests that look inside the bladder [Data: Relationships (1339)].
- **Urinalysis and cytology** — diagnostic tests that study the urine [Data: Relationships (1340)].
- **Resection and biopsy** — diagnostic tests that analyze bladder tissue [Data: Relationships (1341)].
- **Physical exam** — integral component of the diagnosis process [Data: Relationships (1858)].
- **Diagnostic tests (general category)** — used to confirm cancer and support diagnosis [Data: Relationships (3003)].
</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIAGNOSTIC CRITERIA OR CLASSIFICATION CODES (E.G., ICD-10)">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
