      <data key="d4">
**No ICD-10 or other classification codes appear anywhere in the provided data.** However, some diagnostic-criteria-adjacent information exists in the broader graph around AML: specific gene mutations and abnormal chromosomes can support a diagnosis of AML even when the blast count is below 20%, and the source text further states that, in general, 20% or more myeloblasts in the bone marrow or blood is required for an AML diagnosis [Data: Relationships (902, 903); Entities (471, 472); Sources (69)]. These relationships connect to ACUTE MYELOID LEUKEMIA rather than directly to DIAGNOSIS, but they are the closest available data points on diagnostic thresholds.

---
</data>
