    <node id="PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Platinum-based chemotherapy is a specific chemotherapy regimen commonly recommended for use in conjunction with radiation therapy, particularly when systemic therapy is planned as part of the treatment strategy. It is also utilized as a systemic therapy for metastatic cervical cancer, often administered as a combination regimen to enhance therapeutic effectiveness. 
Relationships:
  - Source: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
    Target: RADIATION THERAPY
    Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy is commonly recommended for use in conjunction with radiation therapy, particularly when systemic therapy is planned. 
  - Source: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
    Target: Metastatic cervical cancer
    Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy is utilized as a systemic therapy for metastatic cervical cancer, often administered as a combination regimen. 

