    <node id="RECTAL CANCER AFTER LOCAL EXCISION WITH HIGH-RISK FEATURES OR T2 TUMORS — WHEN LOCAL EXCISION RESULTS SHOW HIGH-RISK FEATURES OR A LARGER TUMOR INVADING THE MUSCLE LAYER, THE PREFERRED NEXT TREATMENT IS TRANSABDOMINAL SURGERY, BUT A SECOND OPTION IS CHEMOTHERAPY COMBINED WITH RADIATION (CHEMORADIATION). THIS APPROACH IS NORMALLY USED FOR LOCALLY ADVANCED CANCERS. IF CHEMORADIATION WORKS WELL, SUBSEQUENT MANAGEMENT MAY INCLUDE FURTHER CHEMOTHERAPY OR A WATCH-AND-WAIT APPROACH; IF SIGNS OF CANCER REMAIN, TRANSABDOMINAL RESECTION IS RECOMMENDED. THERAPEUTIC RELATION: TREATS/MANAGES (ADJUNCT/SECOND OPTION) [DATA: ENTITIES (146); SOURCES (206)].">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
