    <node id="SKIN BIOPSY">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Skin biopsy is a diagnostic procedure in which a lesion or a small sample of skin tissue is removed and sent to a laboratory for analysis. It is the only way to confirm squamous cell skin cancer and is an essential part of testing for this condition. A pathologist examines the removed tissue to determine whether cancer is present. Skin biopsy can also involve taking a small sample of inflamed skin on the breast, which is often used to help diagnose inflammatory breast cancer. In all cases, the procedure is performed to remove a sample of skin and test it for cancer or other abnormal changes, with the results guiding further diagnosis and treatment.
Relationships: None recorded in the provided Relationships table.

---</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d4">ENTITY: SKIN BIOPSY
Description: Skin biopsy is a diagnostic procedure in which a lesion or a small sample of skin tissue is removed and sent to a laboratory for analysis. It is the only way to confirm squamous cell skin cancer and is an essential part of testing for this condition. A pathologist examines the removed tissue to determine whether cancer is present. Skin biopsy can also involve taking a small sample of inflamed skin on the breast, which is often used to help diagnose inflammatory breast cancer. In all cases, the procedure is performed to remove a sample of skin and test it for cancer or other abnormal changes, with the results guiding further diagnosis and treatment.
Relationships: None recorded in the provided Relationships table.

---</data>
