      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A brain MRI scan is a diagnostic imaging procedure used to examine the brain, specifically to detect swelling of the outer layer of the brain, a condition known as leukemic meningitis, which can arise from leukemia. This scan utilizes radio waves and powerful magnets to create detailed images, and it does not use x-rays. The procedure is also described as an MRI scan of the brain that can reveal this leukemia-related swelling of the brain's outer layer.
