    <node id="IMMUNOSUPPRESSION — &quot;RISK_FACTOR_FOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">
**No entity named IMMUNOSUPPRESSION exists** in the data. Moreover, the data supports the **opposite direction** of causation: a weakened immune system due to HIV or AIDS is listed as a risk factor for cervical cancer, and HIV infection "weakens the immune system and can make it harder to clear HPV infection, increasing the risk of anal cancer" [Data: Relationships (2261, 2262); Entities (101, 927, 928); Sources (168)]. The data does not support "HPV infection is a risk factor for immunosuppression."

**Relation type: not retrievable as requested — direction is reversed and no entity exists; the data instead supports immunosuppression as a risk factor for HPV-related cancers/persistent HPV infection.**

