    <edge source="GENETIC TESTING" target="GERMLINE TESTING" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Relation type: includes as type Genetic testing is a broad term that encompasses various methods used to analyze an individual's DNA. Germline testing is a specific type of genetic testing that focuses on identifying inherited mutations. These mutations are present from birth and can be passed down from parents to their children. By looking for these inherited changes, germline testing helps assess an individual's risk for certain genetic conditions and can inform medical decisions.</data>
      <data key="d8">GENETIC TESTING</data>
    </edge>
