    <edge source="HIGH-DOSE CHEMOTHERAPY" target="INFECTIONS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The body is very vulnerable to infections during high-dose chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d8">INFECTIONS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDICAL HISTORY" target="CARE TEAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The medical history is a record of a patients symptoms, medicines, and related health information, which is shared with the care team during consultations. The care team relies on this medical history to help determine the best treatment plan for the patient. In turn, the patient provides details about symptoms and current medications during the medical history process, enabling the care team to make informed decisions. Together, the medical history and the care team form a collaborative loop: the patient supplies essential information, and the care team uses it to guide treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDICAL HISTORY" target="SURGERY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Doctors ask about surgeries during medical history.</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="NCCN CANCER CENTERS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The NCCN Cancer Centers serve as a key resource for locating clinical trials, specifically within the United States. These centers assist patients in identifying and accessing clinical trial opportunities, making them a valuable source of information for those seeking participation in research studies. The entity CLINICAL TRIAL is central to this resource, as the primary function of the NCCN Cancer Centers is to connect individuals with relevant clinical trials. In summary, NCCN Cancer Centers provide a United Statesbased resource dedicated to helping patients find clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="PHASE 1 CLINICAL TRIAL" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A Phase 1 trial is an early phase in the clinical trial process, focused on dose, safety, and side effects.</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
