      <data key="d7">Diagnosis and treatment are closely connected in prostate cancer care. A diagnosis of prostate cancer risk is used to guide treatment decisions, helping the care team determine which treatment is best for the patient. After the diagnosis is confirmed, the care team discusses the available treatment options with the patient, ensuring that the chosen approach aligns with the individuals risk level and overall situation. (Relationship 1800)</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENT (Entity 36)</data>
    </edge>
