    <edge source="U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM)" target="U.S." id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The U.S. National Library of Medicine is explicitly a U.S. institution.

The relationships above constitute the complete set of direct relationships for these high-degree entities in the retrieved data. Many of the relationships involving TREATMENT TEAM reflect multidisciplinary care coordination across diagnostics (biopsy, histology, lab and molecular testing), treatment modalities (chemotherapy, radiation therapy, surgery, stem cell rescue), and supportive care (nutrition, fertility preservation, distress screening, side-effect management) . The NCCN-related relationships show the network's role as a publishing hub and its curation of external resource organizations, cancer centers, and clinical trial navigational tools . ALL is characterized primarily through its subtypes, EARLY DETECTION is linked to breast and lung cancer screening modalities, and CDC is linked to tobacco-cessation resources .</data>
      <data key="d8">U.S.</data>
    </edge>
